  "caveats": [
    "The sign is fragile: a post-reform drift much smaller than the pre-reform year-to-year swings would flip it (relative-magnitudes breakdown 0.14; below 1 means the swings are enough).",
    "The reform covered metropolitan Perth, but the data are for all of WA. A Perth-only effect would be about a quarter larger than measured.",
    "Business counts cannot show who gained. Longer hours may shift sales from small shops to large chains without changing the totals.",
    "Output per worker was seen once before the design review, so that reading is not blind.",
    "Both register records are drafts: dates verified against the WA register; industries and direction not yet reviewed by a person."
  ],
